# UI, UX & Theming

## Icons (lucide-react only)

- **No emojis** anywhere in UI, locale files, or JSX/TSX — not in badges, selects, headings, or comments
- Use **`lucide-react`** for all decorative and semantic icons
- Pair icon-only buttons with `aria-label` (translated)
- Native `<select>` / `<option>` cannot render React icons — use plain translated labels there
- Prefer consistent status icons: `CheckCircle` (active/paid), `XCircle` (inactive/void), `AlertCircle` (warning)

## Intuitive UX

- Guided flows with numbered steps (e.g. batch billing)
- Clear empty states with next action
- Custom `ConfirmDialog` / `Toast` — never native `alert()` / `confirm()`
- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons; keyboard-friendly modals
- Skip link to `#main-content`; `aria-current="page"` on active nav items
- Modals restore focus to the opener on close

## Global font (single source of truth)

- **Never** hardcode `font-family` in components, CSS, or inline styles
- Define the app font once in `src/index.css` via `--font-family-sans`
- The product font is **Atkinson Hyperlegible** (bundled via `@fontsource/atkinson-hyperlegible`) for all UI text
- Changing that **one line** (plus the fontsource import) must update the entire UI
- Use `font-sans` / `font-mono` Tailwind classes only (mapped to CSS variables); both map to Atkinson
- Settings exposes theme (system/light/dark) and font size — not alternate type families

```css
/* Change global font here — one line */
:root {
  --font-family-sans: "Atkinson Hyperlegible", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
}
```

```tsx
// BAD: font-family: 'Inter' in component CSS
// BAD: className="font-serif" on <html> or layout root
// GOOD: className="font-sans" (inherits token)
```

## Dark / light mode

- Support **both** themes; default to `prefers-color-scheme` via Settings → Theme → System
- Manual override (light/dark) persists in appearance settings + localStorage
- Apply `.dark` on `<html>` through `core/theme/colorScheme.ts`
- Every new surface must use OKLCH CSS tokens (`--color-*`), not raw `gray-*` / `blue-*` Tailwind palettes

## OKLCH colors only

Define tokens once in CSS variables using OKLCH:

```css
:root {
  --color-primary: oklch(0.48 0.18 250);
  --color-surface: oklch(0.98 0.01 250);
}
.dark {
  --color-surface: oklch(0.18 0.02 250);
}
```

Map to Tailwind via `@theme` or `var()`. **No raw hex/hsl in components** — only token references. Verify contrast in both themes. Primary labels use `--color-on-primary`.

## i18n

- All user-visible text through i18next
- Add keys to **`locales/es`** and **`locales/en`** together
- Spanish copy: prefer *registro de cobro* / *recibo interno* over legal *factura*
- Keep `document.documentElement.lang` in sync with the active locale

## Responsive layout

- UI must work on **any screen size** — phone to ultrawide
- Mobile-first: base styles for small screens, `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` / `xl:` for larger
- No fixed pixel widths that break on narrow viewports — prefer `min-w-0`, `flex-1`, `max-w-*`, `%`, `clamp()`
- Tables: horizontal scroll wrapper (`overflow-x-auto`) or card layout on small screens; prefer `scope="col"` on headers
- Modals/dialogs: full-width on mobile (`w-full max-w-lg mx-4`), centered on desktop
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44 px; sidebars collapse or become drawers below `md`
- Test layouts at 320 px, 768 px, 1280 px, and 1920 px widths
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
